exports[`crit. 29: a build redo carries the comment, literal, and the preview it replaces 1`] = `
"You are working on a mockup: «MTC app», for Medical Trust Center. This stage is the BUILD: from the approved plan and the visual direction the owner chose, build the mockup as a clickable app the presenter walks through, and deploy it to a preview the owner opens on the phone.\\n\\n## Where things are\\n\\n- The mockup folder, in the owner's Obsidian vault (the documents go here): /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup\\n- The work folder (inputs and code): /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter\\n- The inputs: /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs\\n\\n- MTC APP.pdf\\n- notas-junta.docx\\n- notes-1.md (the owner’s note)\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\n- Write every document in the language of the inputs (if they are in Spanish, the documents are in Spanish).\\n- Do NOT open anything in /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs/private: it is real client data, and only the plan stage may look at it.\\n- Word files: read them with \`textutil -convert txt -stdout <file>\` in the shell.\\n- PDF files: read them with your file reading tool. A PDF with no text layer (a scan) still renders its pages: read it as an image. Only if you still cannot read it, put that in the open questions.\\n- Every document starts with a YAML frontmatter block.\\n- Do not invent what the inputs do not say: what you infer is an assumption, and is written as one.\\n\\n## What the owner chose at plan\\n\\nThe owner chose «Fichero» (c): Cards you flip.\\nIt is described in /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/05-visual-direction.md (its frontmatter says \`chosen: c\`). Build on that one; the others were not chosen.\\n\\n## This is a redo\\n\\nThe owner reviewed the previous version and asked for changes. The previous version is the app as it is now in /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/mockup-app, deployed at https://medical-trust-center-mockup-old-team.vercel.app.\\n\\nThe owner’s comment, literal:\\n\\n> El paso 3 más lento.\\n\\nChange the app in place, doing what the comment asks. Keep what the comment does not touch.\\n\\n## What to read\\n\\n- The approved brief: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/01-brief.md — what is functional and what is simulated, and what is out of scope.\\n- The story, its steps and the pages: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/03-story-and-pages.md\\n- The invented data: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/04-data.md\\n- The visual directions: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/05-visual-direction.md — only the chosen one (\`chosen: c\` in its frontmatter): its tokens and its step → animation table.\\n- That direction's page, the reference for the step that sells it: /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/directions/c.html\\n\\n## What to build\\n\\nIn /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/mockup-app/ build the app (Next.js, unless 03-story-and-pages.md says a PWA):\\n\\n- every page of 03-story-and-pages.md, so the presenter can click through every step in order, from the first to the last;\\n- the step that sells it, with the animations of the chosen direction exactly as its table says; every animation serves the step its row names, and nothing else moves;\\n- ALL the data from ONE file in the app (for example \`data/demo.ts\`), seeded from 04-data.md: no other file holds a name, a number or a date the demo shows;\\n- nothing real: no backend, no login, no calls to outside services; what the brief says is simulated, is simulated in the app;\\n- it works on a phone (390 px wide) and on a laptop, and respects \`prefers-reduced-motion\`.\\n\\nThen \`npm install\` and \`npm run build\` in /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/mockup-app: it must build clean, with no errors. Do not touch /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/directions.\\n\\n## Publishing\\n\\nPublish /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/mockup-app to a Vercel preview, from inside that folder, in this order:\\n\\n1. \`vercel project add medical-trust-center-mockup\` — an answer that it already exists is fine.\\n2. \`vercel link --yes --project medical-trust-center-mockup\`\\n3. Make sure /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/mockup-app/.vercelignore lists \`.env*\`, \`.vercel\`, \`.next\` and \`node_modules\`: \`vercel link\` writes a \`.env.local\` with a token, and it must never be uploaded. And make sure /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/mockup-app/vercel.json says \`{ \\"framework\\": \\"nextjs\\" }\` (or the framework the app uses): a project made by \`vercel project add\` has none, and the deploy would look for a static \`public/\` folder.\\n4. \`vercel project protection enable medical-trust-center-mockup --sso\` — so nothing is public before it is checked.\\n5. \`vercel deploy --yes\` — a preview, never \`--prod\`. It prints the deployment URL (https://….vercel.app).\\n6. Call the tool \`check_real_data\` with your runId. If it is not clear, do what it says: \`vercel remove <url> --yes\`, fix, and start again at step 5. Never skip it.\\n7. Only once it is clear: \`vercel project protection disable medical-trust-center-mockup --sso\` — the owner opens the previews on the phone without logging in.\\n8. \`curl -s -o /dev/null -w \\"%{http_code}\\" <url>\` on every URL you will hand in, until each answers 200. It takes a few seconds after step 7; keep trying for up to two minutes. Never hand in a URL that does not answer 200.\\n\\nIf \`vercel\` fails (not logged in, no network, a quota) or a URL never answers 200, do NOT call \`submit_stage\`: say in your reply what failed, with the command and its error, and end your turn. The owner retries the stage.\\n\\n## Handing it in\\n\\nPass \`previewUrl\` to \`submit_stage\`: the deployment URL, once it answers 200.\\n\\n## When you are done\\n\\nCall the tool \`submit_stage\` with runId \`0192f3a4-5b6c-7d8e-9f01-23456789abcd\`, files [\\"mockup-app/package.json\\"] and a one-sentence summary. If it refuses, fix what it says and call it again. When it accepts, end your turn: the owner reviews it from the phone."
`;

exports[`the brief prompt, a redo: the previous version and the owner’s comment, literal 1`] = `
"You are working on a mockup: «MTC app», for Medical Trust Center. This stage is the BRIEF: read every input and write down what the client is asking for, before anyone designs anything.\\n\\n## Where things are\\n\\n- The mockup folder, in the owner's Obsidian vault (the documents go here): /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup\\n- The work folder (inputs and code): /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter\\n- The inputs: /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs\\n\\n- MTC APP.pdf\\n- notas-junta.docx\\n- notes-1.md (the owner’s note)\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\n- Write every document in the language of the inputs (if they are in Spanish, the documents are in Spanish).\\n- Do NOT open anything in /Users/me/BWR/Projects/MedicalTrustCenter/inputs/private: it is real client data, and only the plan stage may look at it.\\n- Word files: read them with \`textutil -convert txt -stdout <file>\` in the shell.\\n- PDF files: read them with your file reading tool. A PDF with no text layer (a scan) still renders its pages: read it as an image. Only if you still cannot read it, put that in the open questions.\\n- Every document starts with a YAML frontmatter block.\\n- Do not invent what the inputs do not say: what you infer is an assumption, and is written as one.\\n\\n## This is a redo\\n\\nThe owner reviewed the previous version and asked for changes. The previous version was copied here:\\n\\n- /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/_versions/01-brief-v1.md\\n\\nThe owner’s comment, literal:\\n\\n> Más detalle del ingreso por QR.\\n> Y quita la parte de pagos.\\n\\nRewrite the document in place, starting from the previous version and doing what the comment asks. Keep what the comment does not touch.\\n\\n## What to write\\n\\nOne file: /Users/me/Obsidian/01-projects/medical-trust-center/mockup/01-brief.md\\n\\nFrontmatter: \`title\`, \`type: mockup-brief\`, \`client\`, \`created\` (today, YYYY-MM-DD) and \`sources\` (the input files you read).\\n\\nThen these sections, in this order. The first three are lists, and none of them may be empty:\\n\\n1. **Understood** — what the inputs say the mockup must show. Each point names its source (the file, or the note).\\n2. **Assumed** — what you inferred and the inputs do not say. Each point with its **risk** if the assumption is wrong.\\n3. **Open questions** — for the client, short and answerable. A document you could not read goes here.\\n4. **Functional vs. simulated** — what the mockup should really do (navigate, fill a form, filter) and what it only pretends (integrations, payments, messages).\\n5. **Out of scope** — what the inputs mention and this mockup will not show.\\n\\nA mockup is a navigable demo, not a product. For a client of BWR it is shown in a meeting to win the work; for the owner's own project it is a prototype to decide the design, not a sales demo. Tell which one this is from the inputs, and write for it.\\nIn «Functional vs. simulated», mark exactly ONE step as the one that sells the idea: the moment it clicks. Mark exactly ONE step, never several.\\n\\n## When you are done\\n\\nCall the tool \`submit_stage\` with runId \`0192f3a4-5b6c-7d8e-9f01-23456789abcd\`, files [\\"01-brief.md\\"] and a one-sentence summary. If it refuses, fix what it says and call it again. When it accepts, end your turn: the owner reviews it from the phone."
`;

